Betano suspends its Flamengo sponsorship as Brazil's betting ban drags on

Kaizen Gaming's Betano has put its main shirt sponsorship of Flamengo on hold until March 31, 2027, or until Provisional Measure 1,394/2026, which banned fixed-odds betting in Brazil, is revoked — whichever comes first. The deal, signed in 2025, paid BRL 268.5 million (about $46.3 million) per season through 2028. Betano said it had tried to keep the contract alive even while barred from showing its brand on the kit. Flamengo says its 2027 budget now excludes the money and projects a BRL 90 million deficit. The club noted that betting firms put about BRL 1.14 billion into sponsorships of Brazil's 20 biggest clubs in 2025 — on average 36% of Série A marketing revenue.

